# Personal data — the memory block is untracked in full, folders and all.
# A fresh clone therefore has no Profile/ or Knowledge/: recreate them from
# the clean template for a NEW installation. Recover lost populated state from
# an approved backup; blank stubs do not restore knowledge.
Profile/
Knowledge/

# Runtime state written by tasks or tooling. Name the files; do not glob *.json,
# which would also swallow .mcp.json, package.json, and any JSON this project owns.
# [Add the specific state files this project produces.]
*.state.json
*.cache.json

# Scratch and deliverables may hold confidential, non-regenerable records.
# Keep folder notes only; valuable ignored material needs an approved backup.
# Note: because these patterns exclude subdirectories too, git will not descend
# into them, so a later "!Outputs/Some/Subfolder/file" negation cannot work.
# Un-ignore the parent folder first if you ever need one.
Working/*
!Working/README.md
Outputs/*
!Outputs/README.md

# Intake queue — the folder is committed, its contents are not.
Incoming/*
!Incoming/README.md

# Local operations records and credentials (git hygiene, not access control).
OPERATIONS.local.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Confidential retired material, outbox and routing history.
_archive/*
!_archive/README.md
Outbox/
ROUTING_LOG.md

